{"kind":"report","text":"Approved exact head 34d709c6aeaae140a4a6ed9b1dd884d25e1b0f04, resting on all 36 artifacts with README 69bcc8ce first. This closes review dd2a995b for the standalone Lane C package.\n\nArchitecture: approved. The five rule kinds now use a synchronously owned, deeply frozen ReplayContext. Decision.input binds the canonical context, including starting aggregate usage and limits, accounting version, lane purpose, recovery-key authority, carry facts and notify directory. replay() reconstructs the complete call. Notify uses a fresh budget and a retained queue context for retries. Configuration-recovery and mandatory carry conditions remain platform code. One act's evaluate calls must run in order with one meter, as documented; distinct acts may run concurrently. Room must supply the pinned immutable active policy and retain its version for replay.\n\nSecurity: approved for this package. Deterministic require failures still refuse; unexpected engine failures remain retryable failures rather than recorded outcomes. Historical admin evidence is judged by recorded admission authority and current signer/grantor compromise, while current initiator authority is checked separately. Promotion cannot upgrade old evidence; ordinary demotion, removal or retirement does not silently reopen it. Flagged sole-admin approval still reopens when a second admin exists. Ownership pairs support constructor, prototype, _jsonata_cache and __proto__ as path values without weakening the profile.\n\nSimplification: approved. A single explicit replay boundary replaces hidden side inputs and aliased retained input. Path/owners pairs eliminate the reserved-key map hazard. Fresh expression compilation retains evaluator isolation. The sampled CPU estimate is now correctly described as an estimate.\n\nValidation: npm run typecheck passed. The unchanged candidate suite passed all 154 tests on Node and all 154 on workerd, including the original concrete budget/directory, input-mutation, authority and path reproductions. Four additional checker-only tests passed on both hosts: retained budget versus externally mutated limits, directory mutation during await, complete carry replay, and land input mutation plus complete result replay. These tests live only in the detached /tmp/artroom-checker-policy-v2 worktree. The reported mutation spot-checks were not independently rerun.\n\nIntegration follow-up remains required, not waived by this approval: adopt the README's PathOwners[], ReplayContext/Decision.input and versioned aggregate accounting in the contract before Room integration. Resolve the documented contract gaps explicitly; do not revert Room inputs to unsafe maps or omit replay side inputs. The README dependency paragraph is stale now that the contract repair has landed and should be refreshed with that amendment. Full functional scope remains intact; estimates are not approval conditions.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:69bcc8ce746ee22e12a88a808a305c74574b5617","binding":"assigned","head":"34d709c6aeaae140a4a6ed9b1dd884d25e1b0f04","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:63cd07b0f7198d2faaa6a61fda6fcf294a7ef546\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f182d666b11580e68fef19ba9f458008c95b5845\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:63cd07b0f7198d2faaa6a61fda6fcf294a7ef546","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}